// BT-3796 (ADR 0131 Phase 2c): the loop-body producer matrix, one method per
// cell of inner construct x enclosing frames x statement shape x write
// variant, in the class-method, value-type and actor column. Every method sums into the outer local `t`
// inside the inner construct, which sits in the body of the frame (a
// `to:do:`/`timesRepeat:`/`whileTrue:` loop, a `do:`/`collect:`/`inject:into:`
// fold, or two or three of them nested) as a bare statement, an assignment's
// value, a literal element or after a read of `t`; the `plain`, `selfsend`
// and `cvar` variants add a self-send or a field/class-variable write inside
// the construct. A cell Phase 0 rejects (an actor fold frame's value-bearing
// sites) has no method. The expected answers are in
// stdlib/test/adr0131loop_matrix_test.bt.

TestCase subclass: Adr0131LoopMatrixTest

  testClassDoToDoBarePlain =>
    self assert: Adr0131LoopMatrixClass do_toDo_bare_plain equals: #[6, 0, 0]

  testClassDoToDoBareCvar =>
    self assert: Adr0131LoopMatrixClass do_toDo_bare_cvar equals: #[6, 0, 0, 4]

